lf Flush pattern with concentrated Dots suit tiles. By discarding J3, I maintain flexibility with consecutive Dots tiles (B3-B7) and a strong B8 pung, while keeping my B2 pair intact. This keeps me in tenpai or close to it for a Half Flush hand (6 points), potentially combined with other patterns like All Simples (2 points) for a total of 8+ points needed to win.\n\nAnswer: Play J3"}
